WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:04.571
You built the assistants on a test site, and now you need them

00:00:04.571 --> 00:00:05.778
on the live site.

00:00:05.778 --> 00:00:09.034
This video shows how to export the AI setup of a site in

00:00:09.034 --> 00:00:13.340
a deployment plan, and how to import it on another site, in the right order.

00:00:17.940 --> 00:00:23.567
A deployment plan can carry the AI provider connections and deployments, the profiles

00:00:23.567 --> 00:00:27.710
and their templates, the tool instances and the data sources.

00:00:28.460 --> 00:00:32.655
It can also carry MCP connections, prompts and resources.

00:00:32.655 --> 00:00:36.850
Each kind is a step of the plan, and a step exports every

00:00:36.850 --> 00:00:39.380
item, or only the ones you pick.

00:00:40.130 --> 00:00:44.994
The same items can be created from a recipe, which is what a plan produces.

00:00:44.994 --> 00:00:49.198
Knowledge that was uploaded or indexed is content, not settings:

00:00:49.198 --> 00:00:51.600
it does not travel in these steps.

00:00:55.810 --> 00:00:59.565
Open Tools, Deployments, Plans, and click Add Plan.

00:00:59.565 --> 00:01:03.320
Give it a name, such as AI setup, and click Create.

00:01:03.772 --> 00:01:08.633
The plan page lists every kind of step that the enabled features offer.

00:01:08.633 --> 00:01:13.682
Click Add on AI Provider Connections, tick Include all, and save the step.

00:01:14.132 --> 00:01:17.027
Add the AI Deployments step the same way.

00:01:17.027 --> 00:01:21.461
Then add AI Profiles, and tick only the profiles you want to move.

00:01:21.461 --> 00:01:22.693
Order matters:

00:01:22.693 --> 00:01:28.790
connections first, deployments next, and profiles last, because profiles point at the others.

00:01:28.790 --> 00:01:32.485
Each one is saved as its own step of the plan, and the

00:01:32.485 --> 00:01:34.702
plan lists them in that order.

00:01:35.153 --> 00:01:41.556
Add the AI Tool Instances, AI Data Sources and MCP steps when the profiles use them.

00:01:41.556 --> 00:01:46.963
Each step has an Include all switch, or a list of the items to choose.

00:01:51.143 --> 00:01:55.004
On the plan page, click Execute and choose File Download.

00:01:55.004 --> 00:01:58.559
It runs the plan and downloads its result as a file.

00:01:58.559 --> 00:02:00.520
Treat that file with care:

00:02:00.520 --> 00:02:05.423
it holds the settings of your assistants, and may hold connection details.

00:02:05.873 --> 00:02:08.099
The file is a package or a recipe.

00:02:08.099 --> 00:02:11.659
You can open it in any editor, change it, and keep it with

00:02:11.659 --> 00:02:13.383
the rest of your project.

00:02:17.577 --> 00:02:22.925
On the other site, open Tools, Deployments, JSON Import to paste a recipe

00:02:22.925 --> 00:02:26.987
into the editor, or Package Import to upload the file.

00:02:27.438 --> 00:02:31.650
The import creates the items in the order of the file, and updates

00:02:31.650 --> 00:02:33.698
the items that already exist.

00:02:33.698 --> 00:02:38.787
Afterwards, open Connections and re-enter any secret that was left out, and check

00:02:38.787 --> 00:02:41.478
the default deployments in the settings.

00:02:45.678 --> 00:02:48.858
Enable the same features on both sites first.

00:02:48.858 --> 00:02:53.098
A step can only import items that the target site understands.

00:02:53.848 --> 00:02:58.067
Test the import on a copy before the live site, and keep the

00:02:58.067 --> 00:03:00.688
exported file out of public places.

00:03:01.438 --> 00:03:05.134
After the import, run the knowledge steps again:

00:03:05.134 --> 00:03:09.718
sync data sources, crawlers and file sources on the new site.

00:03:11.718 --> 00:03:15.725
Build a plan with the AI steps, export it, and import it where

00:03:15.725 --> 00:03:18.966
you need it, connections first and profiles last.

00:03:18.966 --> 00:03:20.498
Thanks for watching.

